      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg/day**. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a monitored setting (3,200 mg/day), and four times the OTC limit (1,200 mg/day). At that level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, split into smaller doses\n\nTell me which one, or confirm that 1600 mg QID is what you want. If it is, please add a clinical rationale and I'll put it in the order note. I'll enter the order as soon as I hear back."
      }
